N00B_DIAG(LET_ASSIGNED_TWICE, "N00B-S0001", ERROR,
    "a `let` is assigned after it was initialized",
    "A `let` gets exactly one value. Assigning it again, or assigning it on\n"
    "a path where it may already hold a value, is an error.\n"
    "Declare it with `var` if it must change:\n"
    "    var total = 0\n"
    "    total = 5")
N00B_DIAG(LET_INITIALIZED_IN_LOOP, "N00B-S0002", ERROR,
    "a `let` declared outside a loop is initialized inside it",
    "A loop body can run more than once, so initializing a `let` declared\n"
    "outside the loop could assign it twice. Declare the `let` inside the\n"
    "loop, or use `var`.")
N00B_DIAG(USE_AFTER_CONSUME, "N00B-S0003", ERROR,
    "a value is used after it may have been consumed",
    "Passing a value to a `consume` parameter hands it over; the caller\n"
    "cannot use it afterwards on any path. Pass a copy if you still need\n"
    "the value, or stop using it after the call.")
N00B_DIAG(READ_BEFORE_ASSIGNMENT, "N00B-S0004", ERROR,
    "a variable is read on a path where it has no value",
    "Every path to a read must assign the variable first. Give the variable\n"
    "an initial value, or assign it on every path:\n"
    "    var x = 0")
N00B_DIAG(UNREACHABLE_CODE, "N00B-S0005", WARNING,
    "code can never run",
    "No path reaches this code: something before it always returns, fails,\n"
    "loops forever or calls a function that never returns, or a constant\n"
    "condition skips it. Remove the code or fix the condition.")
N00B_DIAG(UNUSED_ASSIGNMENT, "N00B-S0006", WARNING,
    "a stored value is never read",
    "The value assigned here is overwritten or discarded before anything\n"
    "reads it, so the assignment has no effect. Remove it, or use the\n"
    "value.")
N00B_DIAG(UNUSED_VALUE, "N00B-S0007", WARNING,
    "the value of an expression statement is never used",
    "An expression used as a statement computes a value that is thrown\n"
    "away. Use the value, assign it, or remove the statement. Inside\n"
    "function bodies this is an error.")
N00B_DIAG(UNBOUNDED_RECURSION, "N00B-S0008", WARNING,
    "a function calls itself on every path",
    "Every path through the function calls the function again before it can\n"
    "return, so a call never finishes. Add a path that returns without\n"
    "recursing.")
N00B_DIAG(OPTION_NOT_PROVEN, "N00B-S0009", ERROR,
    "an option's value is used where it may be nil",
    "A value of type `T?` can be nil. Test it before using its value, with\n"
    "no assignment to it in between:\n"
    "    if x != nil {\n"
    "        return x + 1\n"
    "    }")
N00B_DIAG(VIEW_WRITE, "N00B-S0010", ERROR,
    "a write reaches memory reachable from a view parameter or constant",
    "Nothing reachable from a `view` parameter or a constant may be\n"
    "written, including through calls. Take the parameter as `modify`, or\n"
    "write to a copy.")
N00B_DIAG(VIEW_ESCAPE, "N00B-S0011", ERROR,
    "a reference reachable from a view parameter outlives the call",
    "A `view` parameter is only borrowed for the call. Storing a reference\n"
    "to it, or to anything reachable from it, somewhere that outlives the\n"
    "call is not allowed; only returning it is. Store a copy instead.")
N00B_DIAG(MISSING_RETURN, "N00B-S0012", ERROR,
    "a function can reach the end of its body without returning a value",
    "A function with a result type must end every path with `return`,\n"
    "`fail`, or a call that never returns. Add the missing `return`.")
N00B_DIAG(SWITCH_NOT_EXHAUSTIVE, "N00B-S0013", ERROR,
    "a `switch` does not handle every possible value",
    "A `switch` on a variant without `else` must have a case for every arm,\n"
    "and a `switch` that a function relies on to return must cover every\n"
    "value. Add the missing cases or an `else`.")
N00B_DIAG(ASSERT_SIDE_EFFECT, "N00B-S0015", ERROR,
    "an `assert` condition changes program state",
    "`assert` conditions do not run in release builds, so they must not\n"
    "change anything. Compute the value before the `assert`:\n"
    "    let ok = bump()\n"
    "    assert ok")
N00B_DIAG(OUTPUT_ARGUMENT_NOT_WRITABLE, "N00B-S0016", ERROR,
    "an `out` or `modify` argument is not writable",
    "An `out` or `modify` parameter writes back to its argument, so the\n"
    "argument must be a `var`, a writable field or element, or a `modify`\n"
    "parameter. A `let`, a constant or an `in` parameter cannot be passed.")
N00B_DIAG(SAME_OUTPUT_TWICE, "N00B-S0017", ERROR,
    "one variable is passed to two output parameters of a call",
    "Each `out` or `modify` parameter writes back to its argument, so one\n"
    "variable cannot receive two of them. Pass separate variables.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSUME_PART, "N00B-S0018", ERROR,
    "a field or element is passed to a `consume` parameter",
    "Only a whole variable or a temporary value can be consumed. Consume\n"
    "the whole value, or pass a copy of the field or element.")
N00B_DIAG(NOT_WRITABLE, "N00B-S0019", ERROR,
    "an assignment target cannot be written",
    "The target belongs to a `let`, a constant, an `in` or `view`\n"
    "parameter, or is a field that is not mutable. Declare the variable\n"
    "with `var` or take the parameter as `modify`.")
N00B_DIAG(TRY_CANNOT_FAIL, "N00B-S0020", ERROR,
    "a `try` has a failure handler but nothing in it can fail",
    "The `fail` handler of this `try` can never run because nothing in the\n"
    "body can fail. Remove the `try` and its handler.")
N00B_DIAG(JUMP_OUTSIDE_LOOP, "N00B-S0022", ERROR,
    "`break` or `continue` is used outside a loop",
    "`continue` must be inside a loop; `break` must be inside a loop,\n"
    "`switch` or `typecase`.")
N00B_DIAG(FAILURE_NOT_PROPAGATED, "N00B-S0025", ERROR,
    "a call that can fail is neither propagated nor handled",
    "A call to a function that can fail needs a trailing `!` to pass the\n"
    "failure on, or a `try` to handle it:\n"
    "    let n = parse(text)!")
N00B_DIAG(PROPAGATE_INFALLIBLE, "N00B-S0026", ERROR,
    "`!` is used on something that cannot fail",
    "A trailing `!` passes a failure to the caller, but this call has no\n"
    "failure to pass. Remove the `!`.")
N00B_DIAG(IF_VALUE_WITHOUT_ELSE, "N00B-S0023", ERROR,
    "an `if` used as a value has no `else`",
    "When an `if` produces a value, every path must produce one, so it\n"
    "needs an `else` with the value to use when no condition holds.")
N00B_DIAG(FAIL_WITHOUT_FAILURE_TYPE, "N00B-S0024", ERROR,
    "`fail` is used where no failure type is declared",
    "`fail` passes a failure to the caller, so the enclosing function must\n"
    "declare a failure type:\n"
    "    func parse(s: string) -> int fail: string {")
N00B_DIAG(TOP_LEVEL_FAILURE, "N00B-S0027", ERROR,
    "top-level code can fail with nothing to pass the failure to",
    "Top-level statements have no caller, so a failure there cannot be\n"
    "propagated with `!`. Handle it with `try`, or move the code into a\n"
    "function that declares a failure type.")
N00B_DIAG(DUPLICATE_SWITCH_CASE, "N00B-S0030", ERROR,
    "a `switch` handles the same arm twice",
    "Each arm can appear in only one `case`. Remove or merge the duplicate.")
N00B_DIAG(SUBJECT_NOT_VARIABLE, "N00B-S0031", ERROR,
    "a `typecase` or variant `switch` subject is not a variable",
    "`typecase` and `switch` on a variant narrow their subject inside each\n"
    "case, so the subject must be a variable or parameter. Store the value\n"
    "in a variable first.")
N00B_DIAG(TYPECASE_WITHOUT_CASES, "N00B-S0032", ERROR,
    "a `typecase` has no `case`",
    "A `typecase` needs at least one `case`.")
N00B_DIAG(ARM_HAS_NO_PAYLOAD, "N00B-S0033", ERROR,
    "the value of a variant arm that carries no value is read",
    "This arm of the variant has no payload, so there is nothing to read.\n"
    "Test for the arm without reading its value.")
N00B_DIAG(VALUE_BLOCK_WITHOUT_VALUE, "N00B-S0034", ERROR,
    "a block used as a value can end without producing one",
    "Every path through a block or expression that is used as a value must\n"
    "end with the value it produces.")
N00B_DIAG(DEFAULT_CYCLE, "N00B-S0035", ERROR,
    "default parameter values depend on each other in a cycle",
    "A default value can use other parameters, but not in a cycle. Remove\n"
    "the cycle, or pass one of the parameters explicitly.")
N00B_DIAG(DEFAULT_ORDER, "N00B-S0036", ERROR,
    "a default parameter value reads a parameter that has no value yet",
    "Keyword defaults are applied left to right, after the positional\n"
    "parameters and the varargs parameter are bound. A default can use\n"
    "those and any keyword parameter declared before it, but not one\n"
    "declared after it:\n"
    "    func box(width: int, height: int = width, depth: int = height)")
N00B_DIAG(CONTEXT_OUTSIDE_WITH, "N00B-S0037", ERROR,
    "a context is called outside a `with` statement",
    "A context declaration is entered with `with`, which runs its hooks.\n"
    "Call it as part of a `with` statement.")
N00B_DIAG(ATOMIC_PART_UPDATE, "N00B-S0038", ERROR,
    "an atomic value is updated one field at a time",
    "An atomic value changes as a whole. Build the new value and assign the\n"
    "whole atomic at once.")
N00B_DIAG(NOT_SUPPORTED_YET, "N00B-S0039", ERROR,
    "the program uses a construct the compiler does not support yet",
    "The language allows this construct, but this compiler cannot build it\n"
    "yet. The message names the construct; write the code another way for\n"
    "now.")
N00B_DIAG(CONTEXT_HOOK_CANNOT_FAIL, "N00B-S0040", ERROR,
    "a context hook that cannot report failures declares a failure type",
    "This hook runs where a failure cannot be passed on. Handle the failure\n"
    "inside the hook.")
N00B_DIAG(ZERO_RANGE_STEP, "N00B-S0042", ERROR,
    "a range loop steps by zero",
    "A `for` range with `step 0` never reaches its end. Give a step that\n"
    "is not zero; a step that is only known when the program runs is\n"
    "checked then, and a zero step stops the program.")
N00B_DIAG(UNREACHABLE_TOP_LEVEL, "N00B-S0043", ERROR,
    "a top-level statement can never run",
    "The top-level code before this statement always stops, so the\n"
    "statement never runs. Remove it, or what stops the code before it.")
N00B_DIAG(OUTPUT_PARAMETER_DEFAULT, "N00B-S0044", ERROR,
    "an `out` or `modify` parameter has a default value",
    "A default value only makes sense for a parameter the function reads.\n"
    "Remove the default, or make the parameter an `in` parameter.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSUME_ESCAPED, "N00B-S0045", ERROR,
    "a value is consumed while references to it may still be in use",
    "Consuming a value hands it over, so nothing else may still refer to\n"
    "it. Pass a copy, or stop keeping references to the value.")
N00B_DIAG(CONST_WITHOUT_VALUE, "N00B-S0046", ERROR,
    "a `const` has no value known when the program is built",
    "A `const` needs an initializer the compiler can evaluate:\n"
    "    const LIMIT = 64")
N00B_DIAG(CONST_READS_RUNTIME_VAR, "N00B-S0049", ERROR,
    "a `const` reads a variable that is set only when the program runs",
    "A `const` is computed while the program is built, so it can read only\n"
    "values set by then: other consts, and variables the initializer sets\n"
    "before the `const`. Give the variable its value earlier, or compute\n"
    "the `const` from other consts.")
N00B_DIAG(MODULE_INIT_CYCLE, "N00B-S0051", ERROR,
    "modules read each other's globals while they initialize",
    "No module in the cycle can initialize first, because each reads a\n"
    "global of another before that global is set. Move the reads into\n"
    "functions that run after initialization, or break the cycle.")
N00B_DIAG(GLOBAL_READ_BEFORE_INIT, "N00B-S0052", ERROR,
    "a global is read before it is initialized",
    "Initialization runs in order, so a global cannot be read before its\n"
    "initializer has run. Move the declaration above its first use, or\n"
    "give the global an explicit initializer.")
N00B_DIAG(OVERFLOW_ALWAYS, "N00B-S0053", ERROR,
    "an integer operation always overflows",
    "For every value the operands can have, the result does not fit the\n"
    "type. Use a wider type, or `unsafe_add`, `unsafe_sub` or `unsafe_mul`\n"
    "for wrapping arithmetic.")
N00B_DIAG(OVERFLOW_POSSIBLE, "N00B-S0054", WARNING,
    "an integer operation may overflow",
    "For some values the operands can have, the result does not fit the\n"
    "type, and the program stops there when it runs. Check the operands\n"
    "first or use a wider type.")
N00B_DIAG(DIVISOR_ZERO, "N00B-S0055", ERROR,
    "a divisor is always zero",
    "Dividing by zero stops the program. Fix the divisor.")
N00B_DIAG(DIVISOR_MAY_BE_ZERO, "N00B-S0056", WARNING,
    "a divisor may be zero",
    "For some values the divisor is zero, and the program stops there when\n"
    "it runs. Test the divisor first.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIFT_OUT_OF_RANGE, "N00B-S0057", ERROR,
    "a shift amount is always out of range",
    "A shift amount must be at least 0 and less than the width of the type.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIFT_MAY_BE_OUT_OF_RANGE, "N00B-S0058", WARNING,
    "a shift amount may be out of range",
    "For some values the shift amount is negative or at least the width of\n"
    "the type, and the program stops there when it runs.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSTANT_CONDITION, "N00B-S0059", WARNING,
    "a condition always has the same value",
    "The values that reach this test make it always true or always false,\n"
    "so one branch never runs.")
N00B_DIAG(DATA_RACE, "N00B-S0060", WARNING,
    "a global is shared between threads without synchronization",
    "A thread writes this global without atomics or a lock while another\n"
    "thread can access it. Make it atomic or guard every access with a\n"
    "lock.")
N00B_DIAG(CALL_WITHOUT_EFFECT, "N00B-S0062", WARNING,
    "a call has no effect and its result is ignored",
    "The called function changes nothing the caller can see, so ignoring\n"
    "its result makes the call pointless. Use the result or remove the\n"
    "call.")
N00B_DIAG(UNUSED_PARAMETER, "N00B-S0063", WARNING,
    "a parameter is never used",
    "Nothing in the function uses this parameter. Remove it, or name it\n"
    "with a leading `_` if a signature requires it.")
N00B_DIAG(PARAMETER_COULD_BE_VIEW, "N00B-S0064", INFO,
    "a parameter could be declared `view`",
    "The function never writes anything reachable from this parameter, so\n"
    "declaring it `view` documents that and lets callers pass shared\n"
    "values.")
N00B_DIAG(REF_NOT_ADDRESSABLE, "N00B-S0065", ERROR,
    "`ref` is applied to a temporary value",
    "`ref` needs storage to point at: a variable, field or element. Store\n"
    "the value in a `var` and take a `ref` to that.")
N00B_DIAG(SWITCH_SUBJECT_UNSUPPORTED, "N00B-S0067", ERROR,
    "a `switch` cannot match values of this type",
    "A `switch` matches integers, characters, booleans, enums and variants.\n"
    "Compare other values, such as strings, floating-point numbers or\n"
    "records, with `if` and `elif`.")
N00B_DIAG(FINALIZED_COPY, "N00B-S0068", ERROR,
    "a value with a finalizer is copied out of a place",
    "A value whose type has a finalizer, or holds one, is finalized exactly\n"
    "once, so it can only be moved, never copied. Only a whole local\n"
    "variable or parameter can be moved. Move the whole variable, or build\n"
    "a new value.")
N00B_DIAG(FINALIZED_FIELD_UNSET, "N00B-S0069", ERROR,
    "`__init` leaves a field with a finalizer unset",
    "A field whose type has a finalizer, or holds one, starts out zero, and\n"
    "the object's finalizer finalizes it later. Set every such field in\n"
    "`__init`, so a zero value is never finalized.")
N00B_DIAG(REFERENCE_ADDRESS_ESCAPES, "N00B-S0070", ERROR,
    "an address from a reference type outlives the access",
    "`ref` of a place reached through a reference type's `.__value` gives\n"
    "the address that type's `__ref_address` or `__ref_address_mut` handed\n"
    "out. That address is only valid while the access lasts, so it can be\n"
    "passed directly to a call, but not stored or returned.")
N00B_DIAG(BOOKKEEPING_WRITE, "N00B-S0071", ERROR,
    "`__ref_create` or `__finalize` writes visible state",
    "Taking a reference and finalizing a value don't count as writes to the\n"
    "value, so `__ref_create` and `__finalize` may only update private\n"
    "bookkeeping fields of their own type. Make the field private, or move\n"
    "the change out of the hook.")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_KEPT, "N00B-S0072", ERROR,
    "an array parameter is kept beyond the call",
    "An array passed as an ordinary parameter is only lent for the call.\n"
    "A function that keeps it somewhere that outlives the call takes it as\n"
    "`consume`, so the caller hands it over, or keeps a copy.")
N00B_DIAG(EFFECT_CHECK_FALSE, "N00B-S0073", ERROR,
    "a check about effects is false",
    "A statement made only of effect questions is a check: the compiler\n"
    "requires it to be true. The notes show why it isn't. Change the code\n"
    "so the check holds, or change the check.")
N00B_DIAG(EFFECT_CHECK_MIXED, "N00B-S0074", ERROR,
    "a check mixes effect questions with run-time values",
    "A check is answered while compiling, so it can only combine effect\n"
    "questions and constants with `not`, `and` and `or`. Put the run-time\n"
    "part in a statement of its own.")
N00B_DIAG(EFFECT_QUESTION, "N00B-S0075", ERROR,
    "an effect question names something it can't ask about",
    "Effect questions name a function, then an effect or one of that\n"
    "function's parameters. Inside a function body the function can be left\n"
    "out, and the question is about the enclosing function.")
N00B_DIAG(EFFECT_QUESTION_IN_WHEN, "N00B-S0076", ERROR,
    "an effect question decides a `when`",
    "`when` is decided before the compiler knows what functions do, so its\n"
    "condition can't ask about effects. Use `if`, which folds the question\n"
    "away once it is known.")
N00B_DIAG(CALLBACK_BOUND, "N00B-S0077", ERROR,
    "a callback doesn't meet the check on the parameter it's passed to",
    "A function can check what a callback parameter does, with\n"
    "`forbids_effect` or `has_effect`. Every call must then pass a function\n"
    "that meets the check, or forward one of its own parameters that has\n"
    "the same check.")
N00B_DIAG(TRAIT_CHECK, "N00B-S0078", ERROR,
    "an implementation doesn't meet its trait's check",
    "A trait can check what its methods do, with `forbids_effect` or\n"
    "`has_effect`. Calls through the trait rely on it, so every\n"
    "implementation must meet it.")
N00B_DIAG(EFFECT_DECLARATION, "N00B-S0079", ERROR,
    "an effect declaration names something it can't use",
    "`effect Name { from: f; handled_by: g; scope: caller }` declares an\n"
    "effect: calling `f` causes it, and `g` takes care of it so its callers\n"
    "don't get it. Both must name functions. `scope` limits how far the\n"
    "effect reaches: `caller`, `package` or `thread` (the default). Only the\n"
    "declaring module can give a scope, and built-in effects always reach\n"
    "the whole thread. Adding clauses to another module's effect needs its\n"
    "qualified name.")
N00B_DIAG(HANDLED_ELSEWHERE, "N00B-S0080", WARNING,
    "`handled_by` is written outside the package that declares the effect",
    "`handled_by` removes an effect from callers, so it belongs in the\n"
    "package that declares the effect. Then everything that stops the effect\n"
    "is listed in one place.")
N00B_DIAG(MARK_REJECTED, "N00B-S0081", ERROR,
    "a value that may carry a mark is passed to a parameter that rejects it",
    "A mark follows data from the functions that produce it, through every\n"
    "value computed from it. A parameter that rejects the mark can't be\n"
    "given such a value. Check it with one of the mark's validators first.")
N00B_DIAG(MARK_DECLARATION, "N00B-S0082", ERROR,
    "a mark declaration names something it can't use",
    "`mark Name { from: f; cleared_by: g(p); rejected_by: h(p) }` declares\n"
    "a mark. `f`, `g` and `h` must be functions, `p` one of their parameters,\n"
    "and a validator (`cleared_by`) must be able to fail. A mark is declared\n"
    "in the module that owns it.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSTANT_ESCAPE, "N00B-S0083", ERROR,
    "a reference to read-only memory is kept where it could be written",
    "Nothing reachable from a constant or a `View` may change. Keeping a\n"
    "writable reference to it, or to anything reachable from it, in a\n"
    "variable, field or container that is not itself constant would let\n"
    "it be written later, so it is not allowed. Keep a `View` instead,\n"
    "which can be stored anywhere because it cannot be written through:\n"
    "    border: View[Border_Theme] = ref border_plain")
N00B_DIAG(OPTION_COMPARED_TO_VALUE, "N00B-S0084", ERROR,
    "an option is compared with a value before it is tested for `nil`",
    "An option may hold no value, so comparing it with a plain value is\n"
    "not allowed. Test it against `nil` first; once the test shows it\n"
    "holds a value, the option is that value:\n"
    "    if count != nil and count == 5 { ... }\n"
    "Two options of the same type compare directly: they are equal when\n"
    "both are `nil`, or both hold equal values.")
N00B_DIAG(FUNCTION_NAME_AS_VALUE, "N00B-S0086", ERROR,
    "a function name is used as a value",
    "A function is only called by name, or referenced with `ref`. To pass\n"
    "a function around, take its reference and invoke it through `call`:\n"
    "    let step = ref twice\n"
    "    step.call(3)")
N00B_DIAG(INLINE_FUNCTION_REFERENCE, "N00B-S0087", ERROR,
    "a reference to an `inline func` is taken",
    "An `inline func` is inlined at every direct call, so it has no\n"
    "address that a reference could call through. Remove `inline`, or\n"
    "call the function directly.")
N00B_DIAG(CONDITION_NOT_BOOL, "N00B-T1000", ERROR,
    "a condition is not a `bool`",
    "Conditions of `if`, `while`, `assert` and `require`, and the operands\n"
    "of `and`, `or` and `not`, must be `bool`. Write the comparison you\n"
    "mean:\n"
    "    if n != 0 {")
N00B_DIAG(UNSAFE_CAST_OPERANDS, "N00B-T1004", ERROR,
    "`unsafe_cast` is used between types it cannot convert",
    "`unsafe_cast` reinterprets integers and plain references. Use `cast`\n"
    "for other conversions.")
N00B_DIAG(CAST_NOT_DEFINED, "N00B-T1005", ERROR,
    "a cast is used between types with no conversion",
    "No conversion is defined between these types. Convert in steps, or\n"
    "use `unsafe_cast` to reinterpret a reference.")
N00B_DIAG(FLAGSET_INTEGER_TOO_NARROW, "N00B-T1006", ERROR,
    "an integer type is too narrow for a flagset",
    "Casting between a flagset and an integer needs an integer with a bit\n"
    "for every flag. Use a wider unsigned type.")
N00B_DIAG(FAILURE_TYPE_MISMATCH, "N00B-T1007", ERROR,
    "a failure does not have the type the enclosing code fails with",
    "A failure that is passed on must have the failure type of the\n"
    "enclosing function or `try` handler. Convert it, or handle it with\n"
    "`try`.")
N00B_DIAG(TRY_FAILURE_TYPES_DIFFER, "N00B-T1008", ERROR,
    "failures with different types reach the same `try` handler",
    "All failures handled by one `fail` handler must have one type. Convert\n"
    "them to a common type before they reach the handler.")
N00B_DIAG(NEW_VARIANT_ARGUMENTS, "N00B-T1017", ERROR,
    "`new` for a variant is given arguments",
    "`new` creates an empty variant; assign the arm you want afterwards.")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_DIMENSIONS, "N00B-T1018", ERROR,
    "`new` for an array is given the wrong dimensions",
    "Pass one positional size for each dimension of the array type that\n"
    "has no size, outermost first.")
N00B_DIAG(ARRAY_EXTENT_NOT_CONSTANT, "N00B-T1019", ERROR,
    "an array size is not known where it is needed",
    "A fixed array size must be a constant known at compile time. Use a\n"
    "`const`, or leave the dimension unsized and pass its size to `new`.")
N00B_DIAG(BUILTIN_ARGUMENTS, "N00B-T1026", ERROR,
    "a builtin function is given arguments it does not take",
    "The message says what the builtin takes.")
N00B_DIAG(CONTEXT_PARAMETER_MODE, "N00B-T1028", ERROR,
    "a context parameter is not an `in` parameter",
    "Context parameters are read when the context is entered, so they must\n"
    "be `in` parameters.")
N00B_DIAG(VALUE_NEEDS_REFERENCE, "N00B-T1030", ERROR,
    "`__value` is used on something that is not a reference",
    "`__value` reads or writes through a `Ref` or `Foreign` value.")
N00B_DIAG(INIT_SIGNATURE, "N00B-T1031", ERROR,
    "the `__init` that `new` calls returns a value or can fail",
    "An `__init` used by `new` initializes its receiver; it returns nothing\n"
    "and cannot fail.")
N00B_DIAG(CONSTRUCTOR_ARGUMENTS, "N00B-T1032", ERROR,
    "the arguments of `new` do not match an `__init`",
    "Pass the arguments that the type's `__init` declares.")
N00B_DIAG(UNION_VARIABLE, "N00B-T1033", ERROR,
    "a variable would hold an anonymous union",
    "A value whose type is one of several types cannot be stored as is.\n"
    "Give the variable a concrete type, or declare a variant for the\n"
    "alternatives.")
N00B_DIAG(RECORD_HAS_CONSTRUCTOR, "N00B-T1034", ERROR,
    "a field tuple builds a record or object that has an `__init`",
    "A type with an `__init` is built through its constructor, so neither a\n"
    "field tuple nor `cast[T]` fills it in field by field. Call the\n"
    "constructor, or write `unsafe_cast[T](...)` when skipping it is\n"
    "intended.")
N00B_DIAG(UNION_DISCRIMINANT_TYPE, "N00B-T1036", ERROR,
    "a union discriminant is not an 8, 16 or 32-bit integer",
